<p class="prose">Two things a worksheet reaches for that have no closed form: where a function crosses zero, and the area under it. Both take the <strong>name</strong> of a function, the way <code>map</code> and <code>iterate</code> do, and both do a fixed amount of work rather than testing a tolerance — so both give the same bits on every machine.</p>
<p class="prose">A root, by bisection. It needs a bracket and says so if it does not have one.</p>
